BND-19: report inflow volumes for the reporting period when REPORT_START is late

The Node Inflow "Total Inflow Volume" and the Outfall Loading "Total Volume"
printed ctx.nodes.stat_total_inflow_vol, which accumulates from START, next
to statistics that updateStatistics() collects only from REPORT_START. On
the first statistics step of a late reporting period, copy those volumes to
routing_stats.inflow_before_rpt and subtract them in the two columns, as the
patched legacy engine does. The flow balance error column still uses the
whole run. When reporting starts with the run the vector stays empty and
the report is unchanged.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply BND-19_swmm600.patch

diff --git a/src/engine/core/SWMMEngine.cpp b/src/engine/core/SWMMEngine.cpp
index 839529d..e976663 100644
--- a/src/engine/core/SWMMEngine.cpp
+++ b/src/engine/core/SWMMEngine.cpp
@@ -5207,6 +5207,11 @@ void SWMMEngine::updateStatistics(double dt_routing) noexcept {
         (ctx_.elapsed_ms + 1000.0 * dt_routing + 1.0) / 1000.0);
     // ...and only once the reporting period has begun (stats.c:445).
     if (stat_date < ctx_.options.report_start) return;
+    // A late REPORT_START: note each node's inflow volume so far, so the
+    // report's inflow volumes cover the reporting period (stats.c).
+    if (ctx_.routing_stats.report_steps == 0 &&
+        ctx_.options.report_start > ctx_.options.start_date)
+        ctx_.routing_stats.inflow_before_rpt = ctx_.nodes.stat_total_inflow_vol;
     ++ctx_.routing_stats.report_steps;
     ctx_.routing_stats.report_time += dt_routing;
     double sys_outfall_flow = 0.0;   // legacy SysOutfallFlow
